  {
    "label": "figure_title",
    "text": "FIG. S1. Physical origin of the critical topological photonic states from the kinetic inversion. (a) In a conventional gapped topological interface, a localized zero mode is generated by a sign change of the mass term m(x). (b) In a critical topological interface, the boundary mode is instead generated by a sign change of the kinetic coefficient κ(x) while the mass remains tuned to the critical line m ≈ 0. This provides a gapless analogue of the Jackiw-Rebbi domain-wall mechanism [37]",
