  {
    "label": "figure_title",
    "text": "FIG. S2. (a) Real-space coupling schematic for the two-leg implementation of the two-dimensional extended QWZ model. Each cell contains two optical modes, Ai and Bi, forming the pseudospin Ψi,n = (Ai,n, Bi,n)1. The four inter-cell links between neighboring cells realize the effective real-space hopping matrix Tx. (b) Phase diagram of the two-dimensional extended QWZ model. The color denotes the Chern number C of the lower band. Solid black curves mark the Chern-sector boundaries obtained from the analytical gap-closing conditions. The solid red curve highlights the critical topological phase boundary M = λ – 2, which separates two nontrivial Chern sectors (C = 2 and C = 1). The dotted horizontal line indicates the cut λ = 1 used in the main text. The two marked points, (M, λ) = (3, 1) and (-1, 1), correspond respectively to the topological trivial and nontrivial critical points studied in Fig. 4 of the main text.",
